	    Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListCount); 
	    
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ does not contain x in new array
	    Debug.Assert(!New_arrListContainsX); 
        }
    }
}
```
The PUT\_RemoveContract method is a unit test method that is used to verify the contract for the Remove method in the ArrayList class. It tests the behavior of the Remove method when a single item is removed from the list.

In the method, several preconditions are made on the old and new state of the array list (arrList) before and after the remove operation. It asserts several invariants about the new state, including the count of the array list (arrList) and the index of the item (x) in the array list.

The method then assures that after the remove operation, the last index of x in the old array is less than or equal to the size of the new array and that the new array does not contain x. The use of Debug.Assert allows for the verification of these conditions in a user-friendly way without resorting to exceptions. By analyzing the output from the Pex explorer, one can easily verify the correctness of the remove operation on the array list.

It should be noted that this is just one type of unit test method for the ArrayList class, and additional test methods could be constructed to test other contracts and functionalities of the ArrayList class. This example provides a basic idea of the structure and purpose of such a test method.

Here, the ArrayList class contract test covers the Remove method contract, which ensures that the list size decreases after removing an item, checks the last index of removed item in the old array, asserts that removed item does not remain in the list, and also proves that the list contains does not return true for removed item. By using these assertions, we can verify the correctness and robustness of the Remove method in the ArrayList class.--------------------            PexAssert.IsTrue(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListCount, @"The last index of x in the old array is greater than the new array size!");
	    // a call where array does not contain removed x and the last index of x in old array is smaller than new array size.
	    PexAssume.IsTrue(Old_arrListContainsX && (Old_arrListLastIndexOfX < New_arrListCount), @"The array does not contain x!");
            // An assertion that "LastIndexOf(x)" returns a value that is less than "Count". 
	    PexAssert.IsTrue(New_arrListLastIndexOfX < New_arrListCount, @"The last index of x in the array is greater or equal to the array size!");
            PexAssert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX == false, @"The array contains x after the Remove operation!");
        }
    }
}
```

